  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS - Colombia (01-Nov-2016-31-Oct-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia, HIV, Empresa Nacional Promotora del Desarrollo Territorial (ENTerritorio)This program has the following goals: Expand the national response to HIV with a vulnerability approach in the context of the National Response Plan to STIs-HIV-AIDS and the Comprehensive Health Care Model in 6 departments (Antioquia, Valle del Cauca, Atl&#xe1;ntico, Santander, Risaralda and Bol&#xed;var) and 7 priority cities (Bogota, Medellin, Cali, Barranquilla, Bucaramanga, Pereira, Cartagena). The objectives of this program are: Expand prevention, HIV testing promotion, and support for access to prevention and comprehensive care for the most affected populations (MSM and transgender women) in 3 priority cities (Medellin, Bogota and Cali)..  Strengthen the institutional capacities of the response agencies (regional and local authorities, civil society organizations, health services) to contribute to effective access for key populations (MSM, transgender women, people who inject drugs, FSWs, people living on the streets) to health services, prevention of STIs and HIV and comprehensive care for HIV/AIDS, without stigma or discrimination in 6 departments (Antioquia, Valle del Cauca, Risaralda, Bolivar, Atlantico and Santander) and 7 cities ( Bogota, Medellin, Cali, Pereira, Cartagena, B/quilla and B/manga)</narrative>
  </description>
